1. What is Flow Builder?
   ->Flow Builder is a Salesforce automation tool used to automate business processes without coding.
   ->It helps businesses reduce manual work, improve accuracy, save time, and automate workflows like sending emails, updating records, approvals, and notifications.
   ->Flow Builder uses a visual drag-and-drop interface to create automation easily.

2. Types of Flows?
  1.Screen Flow
     ->Screen Flow is used when user interaction is required.
Features:
    ->Displays screens to users
    ->Takes user input
    ->Used for forms and guided processes
Example:
   ->Student registration form
   ->Fee payment form
  ->Help desk support form
2. Record Triggered Flow
    ->Record Triggered Flow runs automatically when a record is created, updated, or deleted.
Features:
  ->Fully automated
   ->No user interaction required
   ->Runs in background

3. Automation Ideas (5 Examples)?
  1. Auto Email After Student Registration
     ->When a student registers, Salesforce automatically sends a confirmation email with student details.
Why automation helps:
   *Saves staff time
   *Instant communication
   *Reduces manual mistakes
2. Auto Update Remaining Course Seats
     ->When a student enrolls in a course, available seats are automatically reduced.
Why automation helps:
    *Prevents overbooking
    *Real-time updates
    *Accurate seat management
3. Notify Faculty When Course is Full
     ->When all seats are filled, faculty receives an automatic notification.
Why automation helps:
   *Faster communication
    *Better course planning
    *Reduces manual checking
4. Generate Student ID Automatically
    ->When a new student record is created, Salesforce automatically generates a student ID.
Why automation helps:
    *Avoids duplicate IDs
    *Faster registration
    *Improves consistency
5. Send Fee Payment Reminder
     ->Before fee deadline, students automatically receive reminder emails.
Why automation helps:
    *Improves payment tracking
    *Reduces late payments
    *Saves administrative effort

4. Flow Design Thinking?
  1. Automation Process:
      ->Auto Email After Student Registration
Flow Diagram:
[Student Registration Created]
              ↓
      [Record Triggered Flow]
              ↓
   [Check Student Email Exists?]
          /           \
       Yes             No
        ↓               ↓
 [Send Confirmation]   [End]
        ↓
      [Finish]

5. Manual vs Automated Process?
  Process: Fee Payment Reminder
   1.Manual Process
     *Staff checks student fee records manually
     *Staff sends reminder emails individually
     *Requires more time and effort
Problems in Manual Process:
   ->Human errors
   ->Delayed reminders
   ->Time consuming
   ->Some students may be missed
2. Automated Process in Salesforce
    *Salesforce checks due dates automatically
    *Reminder emails are sent automatically before deadline
Benefits:
   ->Faster process
   ->Accurate reminders
   ->Saves employee time
   ->Improves productivity

6. Reflection — Why Automation Matters in Enterprise Systems?
    ->Automation is important because it helps companies work faster, reduce errors, and improve efficiency.
   ->Businesses handle large amounts of data and repetitive tasks daily. Manual processes take more time and can create mistakes.
Salesforce automation helps organizations:
   *Improve productivity
  *Maintain data consistency
  *Save operational costs
  *Increase customer satisfaction
  *Reduce repetitive manual work
  *No-code automation tools like Flow Builder allow businesses to automate workflows easily without advanced programming knowledge.


